{"changes":[],"role":"implementation","summary":"Planning discussion 2026-08-15 on eka/fnd:rag-db-optimization. Sub-agent analysis: alex-architect (architecture audit of eka-core/eka-mcp source) and althea-product-specialist (product analysis). RAG half: both analyses independently conclude embeddings/vector-store RAG is premature at current scale (659 objects / 907 payloads / 4 projects); deterministic retrieval (ADR-015, ADR-021) is the contract and RAG breaks reproducibility (index state + model version enter the result function); ADR-021 already reserves semantic capability as far-side adapter, never engine feature; cloud embedding APIs conflict with str:self-hosting. Real retrieval gap identified: Knowledge.Search is exact-match only (no FTS/LIKE/partial), and the Context Engine (ADR-021) is not yet exposed as an MCP tool. Recommended gap-fillers without new infrastructure: SQLite FTS5 (built-in) with deterministic BM25 ranking, and exposing context as an MCP tool. RAG becomes relevant above ~10^4-10^5 payloads or for cross-project semantic recall, with mandatory guardrails (hybrid retrieval, pinned model/index version, provenance on results, canonical resolution never replaced). DB half: many-connections premise is a category error for the current architecture — eka-mcp is stdio one-session-per-process (server.go 'safe for one session at a time'), so N clients fan out into N reader processes; WAL already on, busy_timeout(30000), read-only fast path (readers never take the write lock), SQLITE_BUSY retry+backoff tested. req:eka-mcp-production explicitly excludes HTTP/SSE transport and multi-session concurrency from scope, so 'many connections' does not occur in the in-force roadmap. Verdict: document the non-issue with evidence; optional single hardening (query_only pragma on MCP open path); connection caps relevant only if a network transport arrives. Session finding (this discussion): read-path gap — 'eka context --depth engineering' and 'eka get --upstream' fail on any subject whose neighborhood contains units with unqualified relationship targets (store carries 'req:prd', 'str:self-hosting', 'adr:012-...' without namespace prefix; resolver rejects unqualified forms by design, runtime/resolver.go + TestResolverRejectsUnqualifiedForms). This is a live retrieval bug, more urgent than RAG; unrecorded so far (no issue, no feedback draft). Priority: P2 low-priority research, additive, no conflict with in-force plans; concrete value = DB evidence for req:eka-mcp-production. | Open questions raised and answered in-session: (1) accept keep-deterministic + DB non-issue verdict? -\u003e yes, approved by user; (2) approve the fnd at this session or keep draft? -\u003e approve this session; (3) record read-path gap as bug work item + maintainer feedback? -\u003e yes, eka/bug:context-unqualified-refs + feedback draft; (4) FTS5 minimal slice in scope of this research conclusion? -\u003e yes, included as gap-filler recommendation. Additional user decisions: vector DB rejected now (recorded as conditional option), graph-vs-RAG advantage included in conclusion, Obsidian explicitly excluded from fnd scope.","tests":[]}